00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.330
SANDEEP DINESH: With almost
500 sessions at Next 2019,

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:06.250
it's understandable that you
couldn't get to them all.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.280
So if you didn't get
to "Meet Anthos!"

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.230
stay tuned because
here's the rewind.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.790
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.130
Let's jump right into it.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.460
This session is about how Anthos
helps solve three challenges

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.070
that enterprises face--

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.930
minimizing risk,
increasing innovation,

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.100
and growing and
retaining talented teams.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.080
Minimizing risk often involves
creating and enforcing

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.800
complex IT policy,
building robust guardrails

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.100
in your environments, and
restricting where data can go

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.170
and what services can be used.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.850
That's not the fun part.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.920
Developers want to
spend time and energy

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.400
delivering value to customers
and embracing new technologies.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.200
For example, you may want to
adopt a hybrid cloud strategy

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.630
by adding multiple
cloud platforms along

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.700
with your existing
on-prem deployment.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.400
Each new environment brings
unique development challenges,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.630
security constraints, and its
own quirks and idiosyncrasies.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:07.190
The more differences you
add, the greater the risk.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.990
Anthos comes to the rescue with
a unified platform that can

00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:12.870
run across clouds and on-prem.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:16.440
Your team can focus on building
and operating applications

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.030
instead of learning
the differences

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.770
of each environment.

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.020
Anthos is built on
industry-standard open source

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.843
technology, so the risk of
lock-in is greatly minimized.

00:01:25.843 --> 00:01:27.510
Anthos those lets you
manage and control

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:30.700
these different environments
under a single pane of glass.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.490
And with Anthos
config management,

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:34.980
you can define, enforce,
and track policy

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.710
across your hybrid environments
with a centralized Git

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.390
repository.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.430
Along with minimizing
risk, Anthos

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.020
lets you innovate faster.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.840
With Anthos, developers can
write serverless applications

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.970
that run in Google
Cloud, on-prem,

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.790
and even on other clouds
by using Cloud Run.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.640
Your teams can focus on
delivering value instead of

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.220
wasting time with cluster
management and Kubernetes

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.880
primitives.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:00.790
Anthos also makes it easy to
enhance the observability,

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:04.000
security, and control
of containerized and

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.120
non-containerized applications
with the Istio Powered Service

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:07.930
Mesh.

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:10.930
And Anthos Migrate helps
you convert physical servers

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.050
or VMs directly into
containers without requiring

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.900
additional steps,
complexity, or labor,

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.330
making it easy to
containerize and manage

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.280
all of your workloads.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.640
By bringing together serverless,
Service Mesh, and migration

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.910
technologies into one platform,
Anthos empowers your teams

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:31.100
to be more innovative
and productive.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.100
Finally, finding
and retaining talent

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:35.440
becomes much easier
because Anthos

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.560
is based on industry-standard
open-source technologies

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.250
that more and more developers
are interacting with every day.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.140
You can find experts
in the community who

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.090
can start contributing
on day one

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.580
instead of hiring a team
to create and maintain

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.070
complex internal infrastructure.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.540
Skills that are
learned on the job

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.640
are more easily
transferable as well,

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.540
allowing your teams to be more
collaborative and flexible.

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.140
If you'd like to
see the full talk,

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:02.060
check out the link in
the description below.

